  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Exponential trend"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "If a series grows at a roughly constant rate (like compound interest), fit $y = ab^X$. Taking logarithms, $\\log y = \\log a + X\\log b$, a straight line in X. Fit it by least squares to $(X, \\log y)$: $\\log a = \\frac{\\sum \\log y}{n}$, $\\log b = \\frac{\\sum X\\log y}{\\sum X^2}$, then take antilogs."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Constant growth rate → exponential"
    },
    {
     "en": "Fit a line to log y"
    },
    {
     "en": "b − 1 = growth rate per period"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "For a series growing at a constant rate we fit y equals a b to the power X, by fitting a straight line to log y.",
    "kn": "ಸ್ಥಿರ ದರದಲ್ಲಿ ಬೆಳೆಯುವ ಶ್ರೇಣಿಗೆ y = abˣ ಹೊಂದಿಸುತ್ತೇವೆ; ಇದಕ್ಕಾಗಿ log y ಗೆ ಸರಳರೇಖೆ ಹೊಂದಿಸುತ್ತೇವೆ."
   }
  },
